SUMMARY:Excursion to the Bottle Creek Indian Mound Complex
DESCRIPTION:Historic Blakeley State Park takes guests by boat to the Bottl
 e Creek site\, which has 18 earthen mounds built centuries ago by Native 
 Americans and was once one of the largest communities in the Southeast. T
 he site is reachable only by water. Guests board at Live Oak Landing\, le
 ss than a mile north of I-65 in the Stockton area\, and walk about a half
  mile on the island.\nPrice: from $35\nTimes: Saturday 11/21 · 9:00 AM t
 o 12:30 PM\nChecked against the venue's own page on 2026-10-28\nhttps://c
 oastaleventures.com/events/ev-blakeley-bottle-creek-mounds-1121.html
